  "id": "Compound::DB00398 - Gene::1559",
  "verbalization": "Sorafenib is implicated in the pathogenesis of Drug-induced Liver Injury, Mood Alteration Nos, and Leukoencephalopathy, all of which are linked to Cyp2c9 through a series of molecular interactions. The evidence suggests that Sorafenib may induce the expression or activity of Cyp2c9, which in turn mediates the metabolism of various substrates. The lowest common ancestor of these pathways is the aromatic ether class, indicating a shared structural or functional feature that may facilitate the interaction between Sorafenib and Cyp2c9. The presence of multiple pathways involving Cyp2c9, each with distinct clinical manifestations, suggests a broader role in drug metabolism and toxicity. The integration of these pathways highlights the potential for Sorafenib to modulate Cyp2c9 activity, contributing to the diverse adverse effects observed in patients.",
